I would probably sacrifice a bit more in the hopes of getting
Grayswandir. If I got a different artifact or it was taking too much
time, I would try to get Excalibur (not on minetown fountains!) and
enchant that. Snickersnee is good enough for early game so you don't
need to enchant it immediately. However, if you have several blessed
?EW, it may be a good idea to spend one or two even if you plan using
another weapon later on.
As for Excalibur vs Snickersnee details, Excalibur does slighty more
damage to large monsters, has a bigger to hit bonus and provides drain
resistance and automatic search.
The penalties of Excalibur don't matter much: you can't bribe demons
and "monsters without eyes are able to track you as well as those with
eyes" (whatever that means).
